    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green. There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-day owner sign-up limit in the `addOwner` handler of `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the sole `POST /api/owners` endpoint).\n\n**Changes:**\n1. Added a guard in `addOwner` that rejects the create with **429 Too Many Requests** when 100 or more owners have already been registered today:\n   ```java\n   if (countOwnersRegisteredToday() >= 100) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n   }\n   ```\n2. Added the helper `countOwnersRegisteredToday()`, which counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`.\n\nThe check is placed after the field validations/normalizations (so malformed requests still get their proper 400/409) but before the owner is persisted. Since a new owner defaults its `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()`, the 100 owners created by the acceptance test all count toward today's total, and the 101st is correctly rejected with 429.",
